x02-rng-alignment patch 08-cgm-useful-draw (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (i) the random-number stream, the useful draw: the CGM regime classifier's deviate drawn
from libc rand() as SAGE26 draws it. A measurement instrument, not a proposal for Mimic.

SAGE26 behaviour: determine_and_store_regime (R/src/model_regimes.c:63-100), called once per FoF
evolution at the start of evolve_galaxies when CGMrecipeOn == 1 (R/src/core_build_model.c:410-411,
after every join of the FoF and before infall_recipe at :415), loops over the workspace rows in order,
skips mergeType > 0 (:67), and for a row whose mass_ratio = Mvir / Mshock is not <= 0.0 (:74, :77)
draws random_uniform = (double)rand() / (double)RAND_MAX (:94) from libc's process-global stream,
never seeded (no srand in R/src), and compares it with hot_fraction (:95).

Mimic behaviour replaced: the package's classifier sage26_determine_regime
(models/sage26/modules/sage26_determine_regime/sage26_determine_regime.c:236-248, skipping rows with
no galaxy or Type 3 at :239 and ratios <= 0.0 at :170) draws mimic_sage_cgm_regime_deviate(
UniqueGalaxyID, snapshot) (:187), which returns the package's stateless keyed deviate, keyed on stable
per-galaxy identifiers rather than SAGE26's libc stream (models/sage26/shared/sage_keyed_draw.h:142-145:
mimic_sage_keyed_uniform with the CGM purpose salt and ordinal 0).

What the patch changes: only the body of mimic_sage_cgm_regime_deviate in
models/sage26/shared/sage_keyed_draw.h, which now casts its two arguments to void and returns
(double)rand() / (double)RAND_MAX, SAGE26's expression (R/src/model_regimes.c:94); and it adds
#include <stdlib.h> to that header, which the build needs (without it the package's
sage26_determine_regime.c fails with "call to undeclared function 'rand'" and "use of undeclared
identifier 'RAND_MAX'"). The classifier module, its loop, its skips and its comparison are unchanged
(the keyed-draw contract stays frozen for the classifier); the keyed-draw functions it no longer
calls stay in the header.

Predecessor: the launch base 5e91c80866cedb56a23fb8e53d23bb775f40269d with x01's seven series patches
applied in order from a3063d5836ebe86bfe5c96e4cc7fcd27fe177aa1 (01-particle-mass, 02-cosmic-time,
03-written-dt, 04-substep-count, 05-float-halo-state, 06-inheritance-resets,
07-written-halo-values-stacked). None of them touches this header, so the patch also applies to the
launch base alone; with or without 09-creation-draws.patch (the two touch different files).

Reading for i02: no change to sage16's or halos-only's output: sage_keyed_draw.h is private to
models/sage26 and is included only by models/sage26/modules/sage26_determine_regime/
sage26_determine_regime.c (git grep at the launch base). Under the horizontal driver the classifier
would read the same process-global stream, but in that driver's order (snapshot by snapshot across
forests, and per MPI rank), so a galaxy's deviate would depend on the driver, the traversal and the
rank: the patch gives up the keyed draw's driver invariance (Mimic's VISION Principle 4) and
reproduces SAGE26's stream only under the vertical driver in one process.

diff --git a/models/sage26/shared/sage_keyed_draw.h b/models/sage26/shared/sage_keyed_draw.h
index 3b15c70d..bac50726 100644
--- a/models/sage26/shared/sage_keyed_draw.h
+++ b/models/sage26/shared/sage_keyed_draw.h
@@ -50,6 +50,7 @@
 #define MIMIC_SHARED_SAGE_KEYED_DRAW_H
 
 #include <stdint.h>
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 /** Weyl increment of splitmix64 (2^64 / golden ratio) */
 #define MIMIC_SAGE_DRAW_GOLDEN UINT64_C(0x9e3779b97f4a7c15)
@@ -141,8 +142,9 @@ static inline double mimic_sage_keyed_uniform(const int64_t galaxy_id, const int
  * @return  The deviate, strictly inside (0, 1)
  */
 static inline double mimic_sage_cgm_regime_deviate(const int64_t galaxy_id, const int snapshot) {
-  return mimic_sage_keyed_uniform(galaxy_id, snapshot, MIMIC_SAGE_DRAW_PURPOSE_CGM,
-                                  MIMIC_SAGE_DRAW_ORDINAL_CGM);
+  (void)galaxy_id;
+  (void)snapshot;
+  return (double)rand() / (double)RAND_MAX;
 }
 
 #endif /* MIMIC_SHARED_SAGE_KEYED_DRAW_H */
